        "help_success_heading": "You're on the crew list.",
        "help_success_body": "Your email app should have opened with everything filled in. Hit send and we'll be in touch.",
        "model_eyebrow": "THE NATURE FUND",
        "model_heading": "Every sip and bite is part of the circle of life",
        "model_body": "One big loop that keeps on giving, aka. the circular economy. How is this not already mainstream bewilders us. We trust that you've come this far because you have the courage to stand by our mission, and the courage to stand up for all life on our beautiful planet.",
        "basecamp_eyebrow": "INVESTOR ACCESS ONLY",
        "basecamp_heading": "The rest of the map is reserved for those going to Base Camp with us.",
        "basecamp_body": "As much as we are crazy, delusional and try to have fun along the way, we are serious business about Omawild and our mission to preserve ecological systems through the food we eat. Enter your base camp code to unlock the map. Or if you are new here and interested in advising or investing, <a href=\"mailto:invest@omawild.com\">please let us know</a>.",
        "basecamp_code_label": "BASE CAMP CODE",
        "basecamp_code_placeholder": "Your base camp code",
        "basecamp_cta": "Climb on",
        "roads_eyebrow": "PATHS EXPLORED",
        "roads_heading": "What we ruled out",
        "roads_body": "Before coffee there were many ideas. We share this to give you a full window into our worldview and what shapes Omawild. While we try to keep an open mind, we stand by our values so our brand stays true to what it sets out to be. What killed each one is now a rule.",
        "filter_eyebrow": "THE PRODUCT FILTER",
        "filter_heading": "Questions to check off before adding to our pantry",
        "numbers_eyebrow": "THE NUMBERS",
        "numbers_heading": "What we've done. What we need.",
        "numbers_done_label": "WHAT WE'VE DONE",
        "numbers_need_label": "WHAT WE NEED",
        "founder_eyebrow": "ABOUT THE FOUNDER",
        "founder_lead": "Jenny Hsu spent a decade climbing the tech ladder, burnt out, and packed her life up into 18 boxes. Then she went to Bali to learn permaculture. She came back building a food brand around ecological restoration, because living with farmers and being closer to nature taught her how much the world and our planet can heal through harmony with nature.",
        "founder_body_1": "For Jenny, she gave up comfort in every sense of the word to start over, as a complete beginner, in a new country, and in a new industry with no credentials and no network. But quitting isn't really an option, because that means giving up on our future.",
        "founder_body_2": "Her case for food is simple: we eat it every day, and most of it is grown in ways that deplete the soil, biodiversity and ecosystems we all depend on. She also pushes back on the idea that regenerative farming is the expensive option. Conventional agriculture only looks cheap, she argues, because the cost to soil, water and farmers never shows up on the balance sheet.",
